WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.603
 Congratulations, bladesmiths.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.106
Your work has elevated
you to the third round

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:08.107
of this competition.

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:10.243
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.212
so that you can recreate an
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:19.051
And that weapon
is the cinquedea.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:21.221
Developed in Italy
during the Renaissance,

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.657
the cinquedea gained popularity
among civilian noblemen.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.360
This large, double-edged
sword delivered lethal cuts

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.595
in close quarter attacks,
and was worn on the hip

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.498
to be swiftly drawn in times
of threatening encounters.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:35.234
Derived from the Italian
word for the number five,

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.837
the name cinquedea represents
the blade measuring

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.973
five fingers wide
at the base, which

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.575
became an excellent canvas
for intricate artwork.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.211
With functionality in
mind, swordsmiths also

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.879
included fullers to
lighten the weight

00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:48.848
of this otherwise heavy sword.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.950
Although the cinquedea
lost its popularity

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.419
after the 16th century,
it has recently

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:57.590
made a comeback in the video
game "Assassin's Creed."

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.159
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.631
 We're here in my
forge in Kailua-Kona,

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.100
Hawaii, on the big island.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.602
This is going to be
the most challenging

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.370
thing I've made so far.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.572
I don't even know
how to pronounce it.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.342
I'm using [inaudible]
that I got at a junkyard.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.945
I find there's a beauty in
taking something that somebody

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.880
would throw away, and
making it into something

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.281
they'd keep forever.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.316
So I'm trying to incorporate
the rest of this metal

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:27.220
into an integral guard by
bending these pieces down.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.088
I literally do
everything by eye.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:32.291
I rarely measure anything.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.259
You know, so it's not
going to do this perfectly

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.995
symmetrical piece,
but it's going

00:01:36.061 --> 00:01:37.563
to have the had and felt look.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:40.132
They didn't do it back
then on some machine.

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:41.567
They were doing it by hand.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.937
This acute swell is not
comfortable in your hand.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.706
It's like, the opposite.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.008
Got the shape outlined.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.076
I got the fuller started.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:54.414 line:7%
I'm excited to do this.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.216 line:7%
 It's day three.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:59.085
Having to cut a hole in the
back of my forge took some time,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.987
but I feel like I made
good progress on the blade.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.791
I've got it profiled
the way that I want.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:08.093
Feels a lot better
in the hand now.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.997
So now it's coming to the
most challenging part--

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.199
putting in the fullers.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.368
So I've got the
blade in the mill,

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:19.905
and the milling bit is just
skating right over the surface.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.308
It's polishing,
it's not cutting.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.911
So option B is to try
freehanding it with a file.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:28.214
And the file is just dancing
over the surface of the blade,

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.751
so option C is to try to
freehand it on the grinder.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.686
Bet this looks terrible.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.355
This is, like, a perfect
storm of anxiety.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.191
Doing something for the first
time that's very challenging.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.627
How to solve this problem?

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.129
$10,000 on the line.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:48.301
So I use a smaller milling
bit, and lo and behold,

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:49.935
it just starts biting
into that steel,

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:50.970
just the way I want it to.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.438
It's cutting a slot.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:58.510 line:0%
Smiths who are sneering at
me for not forging them in.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.113
 Day three, and it's hard to
sleep because all I think about

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.549
is this sword.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.486
I want to show to the judges
that I'm not afraid of work,

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:09.154
and that I can
accomplish something

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:11.157
that I put my mind to.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:13.292
It's the most important step.

00:03:13.358 --> 00:03:14.927
I'm about to hit a heat treat.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.530
I couldn't wait to do it all
day, and now that it's time,

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:20.132
I'm scared because
it could fail.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:23.035
Worst case scenario,
my blade could warp.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.404
It could crack.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:27.207
And then I would have
to start all over again.

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:35.714
No warps.

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:36.882
No bends.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:37.783
We're straight.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.618
[sigh]

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.787
File tested it.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:42.888
It's hard.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.022
So I'm happy.

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:45.992
This is still a competition.

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.394
It's not like the stress is off.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.463
Anything could happen
at any given time.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.467 line:7%
 It's day four.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:56.703
It's time for the heat treat.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:59.138
My heart is beating fast.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.274
It's just this feeling,
this culmination--

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.909
it's the climax of the story.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.815
If anything is
going to go wrong,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.017
it's going to happen now.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.156
As I'm watching
it, I can visibly

00:04:17.222 --> 00:04:20.993
see it starting to curl over.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.795
If I'm going to keep this blade
straight, now is the time.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.630
Don't you do it.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.966
Don't you do it!

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:27.934
Don't you bend!

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.610
Ah-ha-ha!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:42.748
Boys and girls, we have
got a hard, straight blade.

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:45.051
I'm happy, I'm relieved.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.485
I can finish now.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:49.389
Now it's just a matter
of assembling the pieces,

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.591
getting everything fit and
finished, tight, and square,

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:53.359
and sharp.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:58.096
 Day five.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.899
This is it.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.367
Just kind of Messing with
the guard a little bit.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.104
Trying to make it a
little bit more fancy.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:09.341
I'm feeling the pressure because
David Baker, and J Neilson,

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:12.144
and Doug are going to look
at it extremely closely.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.446
And it's pretty nerve-wracking.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:16.815
But at the end of the day, I
feel confident that my balloon

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.351
is strong.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.219
And I would take it to battle.

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:21.153
What do you think?

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.221
You think you could win?

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.722
 Mhm.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:24.924
 I hope so.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.793
My son, Maddox, and I would
watch this competition,

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:30.563
and now that I get to
show him a sword that I

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:34.133
made for the competition,
we're both in a little dream

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.067
right now.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:36.469
You proud of your daddy?

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.169
 Yeah.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.004
 Give me a kiss.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.242
 The cinquedea was
used for civilian dress,

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:44.910
but it served one purpose--

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.145
to kill.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.346
I will take your weapon
and deliver killing

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:49.415
blows to this pig carcass.

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:50.849
Daniel, you're up first.
You ready?

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:51.617
 Yes, sir.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.130
 All right, Daniel.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.932
On the backhand slash,
it cut all the way

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.568
through and lacerated the ribs.

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:11.904
On the other edge, it
cut the spine in half.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:16.242
The balance of the blade makes
it very wieldable in combat.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.277
Your weapon will kill.

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.444
 Thank you.

00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:20.679
 All right, Neil, you ready?

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:21.414
 I'm ready.

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:22.148
 Let's do this.

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:40.566
 OK, Neil, this is heavier
compared to Dan's blade.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:44.236
But the edges are sharp
enough to lacerate

00:06:44.302 --> 00:06:45.704
the spine all the way through.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:50.076
The base and the weight
allows for a power slash.

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:53.646
Overall, your
cinquedea will kill.

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:54.447
Good job.

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:56.649
Up next is the sharpness test.

00:06:56.715 --> 00:06:59.385
We will test both of
the edges of your blades

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:02.688
by delivering a strike
across these ratchet straps.

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:04.090
Daniel, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:04.924
 Yes, sir.

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:05.658
 Let's do this.

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:16.702
My hand will tend to choke
up all the way to the guard.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.004
There's a weight
distribution that

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.705
basically pulls the blade away.

00:07:19.771 --> 00:07:21.307
Definitely the
sword, on both sides,

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:24.643
is easy enough to slash through
and deliver a slice that cuts

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.612
through all these ratchets.

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.714
Your blade, sir, will cut.

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:29.348
 Thank you.

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.115
 Good job.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.884
Neil, your turn.

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:32.718
You ready?

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:33.385
 Ready.

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:34.120
 Let's do this.

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:44.797
The dimensions of your
handle really fit my hand.

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:48.267
Anywhere I go, it stays
right where it has to be.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:52.038
Your edge easily cut through
these ratchets on both sides.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.272
Your blade will cut.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.139
Good job.

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:55.808
 Well done.

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:58.077
 Gentlemen, to test the
strength of your weapon,

00:07:58.144 --> 00:08:00.746
I'm going to chop into
this ice block four times

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.014
with each edge of your sword.

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:04.116
Dan, you're up.

00:08:04.182 --> 00:08:05.150
Are you ready?
- Yes, sir.

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:05.885
 OK.

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:14.026
Now the other side.

00:08:26.071 --> 00:08:28.541
Well, I don't see any
chipping or warping,

00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:30.909
so the edge held up very nicely.

00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:33.712
That guard is so lean
that as I'm striking,

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.914
the blade wants to
turn in my hand.

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:36.582
 OK.

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:39.050
 But it did a good job.

00:08:39.117 --> 00:08:40.586
Nicely done.

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:42.188
So Neil, your turn.

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:42.921
You ready?

00:08:43.021 --> 00:08:43.723
 Ready.

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:51.197
 Now the other side.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:04.877
This is heavy.

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:07.713
You see the cinquedea
with the multiple fullers,

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.749
and the purpose of that is
to take that mass out of it.

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:12.451
It's not balanced
badly, because you've

00:09:12.517 --> 00:09:15.220
got really thick tang on there.

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:16.756
I see no damage.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:20.225
I can't feel any rolling,
so it held up beautifully.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:20.959
Nicely done.

00:09:21.026 --> 00:09:23.662
 Thank you.

00:09:23.728 --> 00:09:26.198
 Gentlemen, you've both
done fantastic work.

00:09:26.299 --> 00:09:27.766
But in this arena
of competition,

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:30.102
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:36.509
Neil, congratulations.

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:39.979
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:41.280
Dan, it's that time.

00:09:41.346 --> 00:09:44.283
Please surrender your weapon.

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:45.818
 I came here to win.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:48.754
I wanted to win, but Neil made
something that was better.

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.889
I'm going to go home, I'm
going to go back to my life,

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:52.591
and I'm going to go
back to my craft.

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:55.661
I still love bladesmithing.

00:09:55.728 --> 00:09:58.030
 Neil, you picked
a hell of a way

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.632
to tell the world
that you're here.

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:00.899
Congratulations.

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:02.868
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:05.504
and will be receiving
that check for $10,000.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:06.672
What are you feeling right now?

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:08.440
 It's overwhelming.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.410
 Great job.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:15.080
 My son is going to
be ecstatic that I won.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.850
We've been watching
this show on the couch

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:21.186
last season, to me being on it.

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:23.422
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:25.858
That's me.

00:10:25.925 --> 00:10:27.627
So crazy.

